Subject: [PATCH] build: enable the MPEG video parser already requested by WineDMO

The existing --disable-everything configuration enables MPEG-1/2 decoders,
but not their mpegvideo parser. WineDMO's av_parser_init() therefore returns
NULL and selects GE's custom picture assembler. That assembler retains one
picture until the next picture arrives, then tags the earlier bytes with
the later input's timestamps. A 301-frame B-frame fixture returns 101
backward decoded timestamps and one duplicate through both P14 and P15.
The extracted fallback reproduces those counts against P15's real FFmpeg;
sending the same complete packets directly does not.

Enable the upstream parser that WineDMO already selects. Do not add another
assembler, change the sink queue, or adjust timestamps to conceal the fault.
This also affects FFmpeg's MPEG video demux parsing and needs runtime
qualification; it is not a validated fix merely because the patch applies.

Apply to the GE superproject after the crypto and dav1d build patches.
Requires fresh pin provenance and a new whole-file Makefile.in postimage.
No existing candidate pin or prepared tree may be updated in place. P16
review proposal only: not compiled or playback-qualified. Place the flag
after the decoder list so the immutable crypto patch's context stays intact.
---
diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -364,6 +364,7 @@ FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--enable-encoders \
 	--enable-bsfs \
 	--disable-decoder=vvc \
+	--enable-parser=mpegvideo \
 
 FFMPEG_i386-unix_CONFIGURE_ARGS := \
 	--cross-prefix=i686-linux-gnu- \
